Source: libdiginet
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), git, pkgconf
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/FreeMixer/libdiginet
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: libdiginet0
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: protocol library for the Digidesign Control|24 and ProControl
 libdiginet speaks DigiNet, the raw Ethernet protocol of the Digidesign
 Control|24 and ProControl control surfaces, so a Linux mixer or DAW can drive
 one again: motor faders and their touch, V-Pots and their LED rings, every key
 and lamp, scribble strips, meters, the counter and the jog wheel.
 .
 This is the protocol: the frame grammar, encoders and decoders for every
 control, and one personality per desk. It refuses to encode the desk's
 memory-writing message family.

Package: libdiginet-transport0
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: transport layer for the Digidesign Control|24 and ProControl
 libdiginet-transport carries the protocol of libdiginet over the wire: the
 packet socket, discovery, the online handshake, acknowledgements, a keepalive
 that ACKs never starve, retransmit, back-off, latest-wins coalescing and
 display pacing. It never wakes a desk another host is using.

Package: libdiginet-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libdiginet0 (= ${binary:Version}), libdiginet-transport0 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Control|24 and ProControl libraries, development files
 Headers, the pkg-config files libdiginet and libdiginet-transport, and the
 Kaitai Struct grammar of the protocol, diginet.ksy, for building programs
 that drive a Control|24 or ProControl.

Package: diginet-tools
Section: utils
Architecture: any
Depends: libcap2-bin, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: first test of a Digidesign Control|24 or ProControl
 diginet-probe wakes a Control|24 or ProControl cabled to a network interface,
 moves a fader, lights a lamp, writes a scribble strip, logs and decodes every
 key, touch and turn, and ends with a summary of what the desk answered. It is
 given the one capability it needs to open a packet socket, cap_net_raw, on
 install.
